      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Translation Provider**\n\nI'm currently focused on selecting a concrete, identifiable external provider for the translation task within the `translate_markup.py` script. The goal is to translate HTML/markup while ensuring all the tags are preserved, which influences the choice of a suitable translation service. I'm exploring different options to identify the best fit.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Translation Source**\n\nI've decided on Google Cloud Translation API as the translation provider, ensuring a robust and identifiable service. I'm focusing on the `translate_markup.py` script, planning to use the Google Cloud Translation API client library within the code for clarity and direct interaction. The core logic involves parsing the HTML/markup, extracting translatable text nodes, translating them using the API, and then reconstructing the markup.\n\n\n**Constructing Script Content**\n\nI'm now generating the content for `translate_markup.py`. I've defined a function, `translate_html_markup`, that takes HTML, source, and target languages. I'm initializing the Google Cloud Translation client and preparing to parse the HTML using BeautifulSoup. I'll iterate through text nodes, translate with the API, and replace the original text. My focus is on concise, self-contained code.\n\n\n",
